  "appAsarSha256": "0b5549d1581845ea794c93d0707687ec787bb4fe84b1d63e40f9d0265ac80ea9",
  "fixture": "Neutral fixture drives only. Work files: a local drive created through the New menu with neutral text files, one kept offline. Photos: a New Docker Hub drive in the public test repository mfe-leftovers-test with two short text files, then 800 MB of random bytes for the percentage and another 800 MB pending at quit for the Finishing backup prompt.",
  "captureMethod": "Playwright driving the packaged Electron app in a fresh isolated profile with a hidden, unfocused, off-screen window. The quit prompt is the app's own Material dialog window, captured the same way.",
  "privacy": "Grey screenshot masks cover the signed-in Docker Hub account name, repository names that contain it and profile folder paths; only visible matches are masked.",
  "notCaptured": [
    "The Docker Hub device sign-in code screen: reaching the code needs the real credential store, which holds the account sign-in.",
    "A backup percentage: two packaged-build runs backed up 800 MB and 1 GB of random bytes to the test repository while polling the automatic backup status every quarter second and the status bar text every fifth of a second, and neither run saw a value between 0 and the total. The upload step counts each object when it is read (src/main/registry-sync-service.js), and the objects are read before the slow network transfer, so the count reaches the total almost at once. A percentage that tracks the transfer itself is an open problem, not only a capture gap."
  ],
